"""Slugify text using Claude Code's own encoding scheme.

Every character that is not ASCII alnum becomes exactly one '-' -- no
squeezing runs, no case folding, no path semantics (unlike claude-path,
this never resolves '.'/'..'/trailing-slash -- pure text, safe for titles).

The encoding itself lives in `claude-code-slug` on PyPI, because four
skills here and git-localhost-store all have to agree about it, and copies
of one regex agree only until someone edits one of them. A PEP 723 header
rather than a repo dependency: the callers reach this by relative path
from a checkout, so it must work without anyone having synced a venv.

Usage: claude-slug TEXT
"""

from claude_code_slug.slug import main

raise SystemExit(main())
